  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_002 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat, acc=0.6287). RNA is clearly the dominant signal (RNA-only=0.5907 vs image-only=0.3275), and the multimodal gain over RNA-only is modest (~0.04). We have only tested PCA (a linear encoder) for RNA, leaving open whether a learned encoder (scvi_n200) captures nonlinear structure that PCA misses. Question: config_042 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while keeping the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (concat) identical to config_002, giving a clean single-variable test of RNA representation quality. Why this is the best next experiment: Because RNA is the primary driver of performance, improving its representation has the highest expected impact. A positive result would justify further exploration of learned RNA encoders (e.g., scgpt) and potentially larger multimodal gains; a null result would confirm PCA sufficiency and redirect effort toward profile setting or fusion strategy. This is a high-information, low-confound experiment that directly extends the current best configuration."
}

